[
  {
    "uid": "C0689",
    "text": "Justinian's legal collection describes slavery as contrary to nature while continuing to regulate it. A stated principle therefore conflicts with the institution that the same law upholds.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2990,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-law-nature-tension",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0690",
    "text": "Law upholds what it calls contrary to nature",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2991,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-law-nature-tension",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0691",
    "text": "Roman manumission legally changes an individual from enslaved to freed status. The institution of slavery can remain in place even though this person's status changes.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2992,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-status-changed",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0692",
    "text": "An enslaved person becomes a freed person",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2993,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-status-changed",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0693",
    "text": "A route for freeing individuals leaves slavery as an institution in place. Relief within a system differs from ending the system.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2994,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-reform-not-abolition",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0694",
    "text": "An individual route to freedom is not abolition",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2995,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-reform-not-abolition",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0695",
    "text": "The emperor's collection selects which older law is authoritative. Unlike an edition that displays variants, it also determines which text has legal force.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2996,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-authoritative-lawbook",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0696",
    "text": "Older law edited under imperial authority",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2997,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-authoritative-lawbook",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0697",
    "text": "Medieval scholars at Bologna annotate Justinian's older law. Their commentary gives it new uses and meanings rather than simply continuing the sixth-century empire unchanged.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2998,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-interpreted-law",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0698",
    "text": "Inherited Roman law gains a medieval commentary",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 2999,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-interpreted-law",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0699",
    "text": "Hobbes makes protection a central purpose of political authority. This answers the question of political benefit differently from the ancient accounts.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3000,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-protection-purpose",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0700",
    "text": "Hobbes makes protection a purpose of common power",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3001,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-protection-purpose",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0701",
    "text": "Hobbes argues that authorized sovereign power can secure peace. The argument does not prove that concentrated power always succeeds.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3002,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-hobbes-authority",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0702",
    "text": "Hobbes: authorized sovereign power secures peace",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3003,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-hobbes-authority",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0703",
    "text": "Hobbes grounds political obedience in the sovereign's power to protect. If that protection is lost, the subject's duty can end. Merely disliking a decision is not the same condition.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3004,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-protection-boundary",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0704",
    "text": "Hobbes: lost protection can end obedience",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3005,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-protection-boundary",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0705",
    "text": "Locke grounds legitimate government in consent. Sharing humanity is not itself the same as consenting to a particular political authority.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3006,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-consent-government",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0706",
    "text": "Locke: legitimate government rests on consent",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3007,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-consent-government",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0707",
    "text": "Locke argues that a government's breach of trust can justify resistance. This does not guarantee success or imply that everyone then had an equal vote.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3008,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-resistance",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0708",
    "text": "Locke: breach of trust can justify resistance",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3009,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-resistance",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0709",
    "text": "Hobbes emphasizes authorized power and protection; Locke emphasizes consent, trust and resistance to its breach. They offer different limits on authority, not one agreed social-contract doctrine.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3010,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-rival-contracts",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0710",
    "text": "Protection and resistance yield rival accounts of authority",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3011,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-rival-contracts",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0711",
    "text": "Enslaved insurgents make freedom an active political demand. They are agents of change, not passive recipients of European ideas.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3012,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-emancipation-demand",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0712",
    "text": "Insurgents make freedom a political demand",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3013,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-emancipation-demand",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0713",
    "text": "During the revolution in Saint-Domingue, uprising, war and political pressure lead to abolition decrees. Emancipation becomes law, while enforcement and freedom in daily life remain further questions.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3014,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-emancipation-enacted",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0714",
    "text": "Emancipation becomes law amid revolution",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3015,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-emancipation-enacted",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0715",
    "text": "The 1801 constitution rejects slavery but retains Saint-Domingue's connection with France. Abolition and independence are therefore distinct political achievements.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3016,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-abolition-in-empire",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0716",
    "text": "Abolition is claimed inside the French empire",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3017,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-abolition-in-empire",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0717",
    "text": "Compulsory plantation work prevents people from freely choosing their work. It puts the ideal of consent in conflict with the actual working arrangement.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3018,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-work-consent",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0718",
    "text": "Compulsory cultivation challenges consent",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3019,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-work-consent",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0719",
    "text": "The 1801 constitution rejects slavery while maintaining compulsory plantation work. This exposes a limit on freedom at work without erasing the achievement of emancipation.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3020,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-freedom-practice",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0720",
    "text": "Abolition coexists with coercive labour",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3021,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-freedom-practice",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0721",
    "text": "Haiti's independence breaks France's claim to rule and defends emancipation. It does not remove every form of coercion or secure immediate international recognition.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3022,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-independent-abolition",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0722",
    "text": "An independent state defends emancipation",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3023,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-independent-abolition",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0723",
    "text": "Saint-Domingue's abolition did not automatically end compulsory work. The imagined shared-resource institution therefore needs a way for people to challenge coercive rules, not just a formal promise of freedom.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3024,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-rights-in-practice",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0724",
    "text": "A commons must let people challenge coercive rules",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3025,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-civ-rights-in-practice",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0725",
    "text": "Perspective represents a scene from one fixed eye position. It can make a convincing view without showing the whole place.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3026,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-linear-perspective",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0726",
    "text": "A single-viewpoint perspective",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3027,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-linear-perspective",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0727",
    "text": "The chart helps a navigator follow compass directions. It does not preserve every area's size and shape.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3028,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-bearing-chart",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0728",
    "text": "A chart made for compass bearings",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3029,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-bearing-chart",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0729",
    "text": "Flashes simultaneous by platform clocks reach the moving train midpoint at different times. This establishes different arrival times. To infer emission times in the train frame, the equal distances and speed of light there must also be considered.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3030,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder body",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-unequal-passenger-reception",
        "field": "text"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0730",
    "text": "The moving midpoint receives platform-simultaneous flashes separately",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 3031,
        "world": "atlas-focused-sessions-v6",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-atlas-unequal-passenger-reception",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0731",
    "text": "Divinity: Disputed Questions",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4314,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "chooser",
        "owner": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "field": "title"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0732",
    "text": "A manuscript desk, not a test of faith. Follow a wound, a failed promise, bread, a hungry household and a request for prayer through changing arguments. Build what each writer is claiming, test it against a case, and leave real disagreements open. New chapters reuse distinctions you have made; Read offers short explanations, not a hidden recipe book.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4315,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "chooser",
        "owner": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "field": "premise"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0733",
    "text": "Case: a cut body has lost its health",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4316,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "cut-body",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0734",
    "text": "Imagine an injured person. The body remains, but it is not as sound as it should be. Nothing here says that the injured person deserves the injury.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4317,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "cut-body",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0735",
    "text": "Case: the wound heals; no evil thing escapes",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4318,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "healed-body",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0736",
    "text": "The injury disappears as the body heals. This is Augustine\u2019s kind of example: the loss is repaired, rather than a second material being removed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4319,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "healed-body",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0737",
    "text": "Case: I take the meal my neighbour needs",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4320,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "stolen-meal",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0738",
    "text": "Imagine taking another person\u2019s share for your own comfort, knowing whose share it is. This is a deliberate action, unlike merely suffering a wound.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4321,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "stolen-meal",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0739",
    "text": "Comfort is good; my neighbour is still owed food",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4322,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "fair-share",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0740",
    "text": "Enjoying food is good, but the neighbour is still owed their share. The wrong is taking that food, not enjoying a meal.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4323,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "fair-share",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0741",
    "text": "Genesis: creation was \u201cvery good\u201d",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4324,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "creation-good",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0742",
    "text": "Augustine accepts the goodness of creation as a religious starting point. The wound example does not establish that starting point.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4325,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "creation-good",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0743",
    "text": "A wound is missing health, not an extra substance",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4326,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "health-lost",
        "field": "label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0744",
    "text": "The body is still there, but its health has been damaged. Calling the wound a loss does not make its pain unreal.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4327,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "health-lost",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0745",
    "text": "The wrong is taking what another is owed",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4328,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "choice-unfair",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4740,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-choice-unfair",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0746",
    "text": "Enjoying food and being able to choose are not themselves wrong. The wrong choice is taking food that another person is owed.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4329,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "reader-body",
        "owner": "choice-unfair",
        "field": "reading.text ?? description"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0747",
    "text": "Being hurt is not the same as doing wrong",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4330,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "tile/reader-caption",
        "owner": "harm-not-guilt",
        "field": "label"
      },
      {
        "row": 4742,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
        "surface": "wonder italic caption",
        "owner": "plain-divinity-harm-not-guilt",
        "field": "item.label"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "uid": "C0748",
    "text": "A wound is harm suffered; stealing the meal is a wrong deliberately chosen. Comparing them as losses must not turn suffering into evidence of guilt.",
    "occurrences": [
      {
        "row": 4331,
        "world": "divinity-final-reading-scenes-v7",
